---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Loft Conversion March Cambridgeshire | Truleum Specialists"
  description="Expert loft conversion services in March, Cambridgeshire. Local team for dormer, Velux and bespoke loft builds across March and the Fenland district."
>

  <main class="main-content area-march-page" style="font-family: 'Poppins', Arial, sans-serif;">

    <style>
      .area-march-page {
        --area-blue: #0a1a4a;
        --area-blue-2: #162b70;
        --area-gold: #c9902e;
        --area-soft: #f5f7fb;
        --area-text: #334155;
        overflow-x: hidden;
      }
      .area-wrap { width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 40px)); margin: 0 auto; }
      .area-march-page section,
      .area-march-page h1,
      .area-march-page h2,
      .area-march-page h3,
      .area-march-page p,
      .area-march-page img,
      .area-march-page a { opacity: 1 !important; transform: none !important; }
      .area-hero { padding: 112px 0 96px; color: #fff; background: radial-gradient(circle at 85% 15%, rgba(212,175,55,0.24) 0%, rgba(212,175,55,0) 45%), linear-gradient(132deg, #08163d 0%, #0a1a4a 45%, #1c347f 100%); }
      .area-hero-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.08fr 0.92fr; gap: 40px; align-items: center; }
      .area-kicker { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,232,159,0.98); color: #0a1a4a; border-radius: 999px; padding: 10px 18px; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.6px; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 20px; }
      .area-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(36px, 5vw, 58px); line-height: 1.1; color: #fff; margin: 0 0 18px; max-width: 15ch; }
      .area-hero p { font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.8; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.92); margin: 0 0 26px; max-width: 60ch; }
      .area-hero-actions { display: flex; gap: 14px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 28px; }
      .area-btn { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; text-decoration: none; border-radius: 999px; font-weight: 700; font-size: 15px; padding: 14px 24px; }
      .area-btn-primary { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ffe89f 0%, #9f7628 100%); color: #111827; }
      .area-btn-ghost { color: #fff; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.4); background: rgba(255,255,255,0.08); }
      .lc-metrics { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 16px; margin-top: 8px; }
      .lc-metric { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.16); border-radius: 14px; padding: 16px; text-align: center; }
      .lc-metric strong { display: block; font-size: 24px; line-height: 1; color: #ffe89f; margin-bottom: 6px; }
      .lc-metric span { font-size: 13px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.84); }
      .area-hero-card { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.11); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.16); border-radius: 20px; padding: 18px; backdrop-filter: blur(8px); }
      .area-hero-card img { width: 100%; border-radius: 12px; aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; object-fit: cover; }
      .area-price { margin-top: 14px; background: #fff; border-radius: 12px; padding: 12px 14px; color: #0a1a4a; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; }
      .area-price strong { color: #111827; font-size: 19px; }
      .area-section { padding: 86px 0; }
      .area-head { text-align: center; max-width: 830px; margin: 0 auto 34px; }
      .area-head h2 { color: var(--area-blue); font-size: clamp(30px, 4vw, 44px); line-height: 1.2; margin: 0 0 12px; }
      .area-head p { color: #475569; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.8; margin: 0; }
      .area-intro { background: var(--area-soft); }
      .area-columns { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 26px; }
      .area-panel { background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e4e9f2; border-radius: 16px; padding: 24px; box-shadow: 0 10px 24px rgba(15,23,42,0.05); }
      .area-panel h3 { color: var(--area-blue); font-size: 24px; margin: 0 0 10px; }
      .area-panel p { color: var(--area-text); line-height: 1.8; margin: 0 0 14px; }
      .area-list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 9px; }
      .area-list li { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 9px; color: #1f2937; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 15px; }
      .area-list i { color: var(--area-gold); margin-top: 3px; }
      .area-types-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 18px; }
      .area-type { border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 14px; background: #fff; padding: 20px; }
      .area-type h3 { font-size: 21px; color: var(--area-blue); margin: 0 0 8px; }
      .area-type p { margin: 0; color: var(--area-text); line-height: 1.75; font-size: 15px; }
      .area-zone { background: linear-gradient(180deg, #0a1a4a 0%, #102559 100%); }
      .area-zone .area-head h2, .area-zone .area-head p { color: #fff; }
      .area-zone-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 14px; }
      .area-zone-item { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.15); border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px; }
      .area-zone-item h3 { color: #ffe89f; font-size: 20px; margin: 0 0 8px; }
      .area-zone-item h3 a { color: #ffe89f; text-decoration: none; }
      .area-zone-item h3 a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
      .area-zone-item p { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.9); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0; }
      .area-proof-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 16px; }
      .area-proof { background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 14px; text-align: center; padding: 20px; }
      .area-proof i { color: var(--area-gold); font-size: 24px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
      .area-proof h3 { color: var(--area-blue); font-size: 18px; margin: 0 0 7px; }
      .area-proof p { margin: 0; color: #475569; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.7; }
      .area-faq { background: var(--area-soft); }
      .area-faq-grid { max-width: 920px; margin: 0 auto; display: grid; gap: 12px; }
      .area-faq-item { background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px; }
      .area-faq-item h3 { color: var(--area-blue); margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 19px; }
      .area-faq-item p { margin: 0; color: #334155; line-height: 1.75; font-size: 15px; }
      .area-cta { padding: 88px 0; text-align: center; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0a1a4a 0%, #1f3a8a 100%); }
      .area-cta h2 { color: #fff; margin: 0 0 12px; font-size: clamp(30px, 4vw, 46px); }
      .area-cta p { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.9); max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto 24px; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 17px; }
      @media (max-width: 1080px) { .area-types-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } .area-zone-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } .area-proof-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
      @media (max-width: 900px) { .area-hero { padding: 86px 0 70px; } .area-hero-grid, .area-columns { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .area-hero h1 { max-width: 100%; } }
      @media (max-width: 680px) { .lc-metrics { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .area-section, .area-cta { padding: 64px 0; } .area-types-grid, .area-zone-grid, .area-proof-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .area-head p, .area-hero p, .area-cta p { font-size: 16px; } }
    </style>

    <section class="area-hero">
      <div class="area-wrap area-hero-grid">
        <div>
          <span class="area-kicker"><i class="fas fa-location-dot"></i> March, Cambridgeshire</span>
          <h1>Loft Conversion March Cambridgeshire Homes</h1>
          <p>Need a loft conversion in March, Cambridgeshire? We work with the mix of older terraces, interwar semis and postwar housing found across March and the wider Fenland area. Every project is planned around your specific roof structure, planning situation and goals. See our <a href="/services/loft-conversion-cambridge-service/" style="color:#ffe89f; font-weight:600;">Loft Conversion Service page</a> for full details.</p>
          <div class="area-hero-actions">
            <a href="/contact/" class="area-btn area-btn-primary">Get Free Survey <i class="fas fa-arrow-right"></i></a>
            <a href="/gallery/" class="area-btn area-btn-ghost">View Our Work</a>
          </div>
          <div class="lc-metrics">
            <div class="lc-metric"><strong><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i></strong><span>Free Site Survey</span></div>
            <div class="lc-metric"><strong><i class="fas fa-shield-alt"></i></strong><span>Fully Insured</span></div>
            <div class="lc-metric"><strong><i class="fas fa-award"></i></strong><span>Quality Assured</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="area-hero-card">
          <img src="/wp-content/uploads/Loft-Conversion/loft-service-cambridgeshire.webp" alt="Loft conversion in March Cambridgeshire by Truleum">
          <div class="area-price">
            <span>Typical project budget</span>
            <strong>From £26,000</strong>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="area-section area-intro">
      <div class="area-wrap">
        <div class="area-head">
          <h2>Local Approach For Every Loft Conversion In March</h2>
          <p>We plan each March loft conversion around the specific roof type, planning context and how the room needs to work for your family. Our <a href="/loft-conversion-cambridge-guide-for-homeowners/" style="color: var(--area-blue); font-weight:600;">homeowner guide</a> walks through the full process step by step.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="area-columns">
          <article class="area-panel">
            <h3>What You Get</h3>
            <p>Your March loft conversion includes structural build, insulation, windows, first and second fix electrics and a complete quality finish ready for use.</p>
            <ul class="area-list">
              <li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Clear written quote with stage by stage pricing</li>
              <li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Regular updates through the build from survey to completion</li>
              <li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Layout options for bedrooms, home offices or storage</li>
              <li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Building regulations support through to final sign off</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="area-panel">
            <h3>Why March Homes Need Specialist Input</h3>
            <p>March has a range of traditional Fenland housing including pre-war terraces and semis that each require careful structural assessment. Getting the design and planning right from the start avoids problems later. See the <a href="https://www.planningportal.co.uk/permission/common-projects/loft-conversion" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">Planning Portal</a> for permitted development guidance.</p>
            <ul class="area-list">
              <li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Experience with traditional Fenland terraces and semis</li>
              <li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Structural assessment before any commitment is made</li>
              <li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Design to maximise useful headroom and floor area</li>
              <li><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> Efficient build management to keep disruption low</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="area-section">
      <div class="area-wrap">
        <div class="area-head">
          <h2>Popular Loft Conversion Types For March Properties</h2>
          <p>We assess your roof and recommend what will work best for your home and budget. See our <a href="/loft-conversion-glossary/" style="color: var(--area-blue); font-weight:600;">glossary</a> for plain language explanations of each type.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="area-types-grid">
          <article class="area-type">
            <h3>Dormer Conversion</h3>
            <p>Widely used for March terraces and semis. Creates strong headroom and usable floor area for a bedroom, bathroom or home working space.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="area-type">
            <h3>Velux Conversion</h3>
            <p>A cost effective option using roof windows. Well suited to properties where the roofline is not to be altered and budget is a key consideration.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="area-type">
            <h3>Hip To Gable</h3>
            <p>Good option for end of terrace and semi detached homes wanting wider room proportions without a full rear dormer.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="area-section area-zone">
      <div class="area-wrap">
        <div class="area-head">
          <h2>Areas We Cover Around March</h2>
          <p>We serve March and the wider Fenland district with consistent quality loft conversions and clear project management throughout.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="area-zone-grid">
          <article class="area-zone-item"><h3>March Town Centre</h3><p>Traditional terraces, interwar semis and postwar housing across the Fenland market town.</p></article>
          <article class="area-zone-item"><h3>Whittlesey</h3><p>Neighbouring Fenland town with a similar mix of period and 20th century housing stock.</p></article>
          <article class="area-zone-item"><h3>Chatteris and Manea</h3><p>Fenland communities south of March with traditional residential streets.</p></article>
          <article class="area-zone-item"><h3>Wimblington and Doddington</h3><p>Villages within the March area with a mix of older and newer properties.</p></article>
          <article class="area-zone-item"><h3><a href="/loft-conversion-peterborough/">Peterborough</a></h3><p>City coverage to the northwest including all Peterborough districts and suburbs.</p></article>
          <article class="area-zone-item"><h3><a href="/loft-conversion-wisbech/">Wisbech</a></h3><p>Port town to the north with period housing and 20th century residential areas.</p></article>
          <article class="area-zone-item"><h3><a href="/loft-conversion-ely/">Ely</a></h3><p>Cathedral city coverage southeast of March across Fenland communities.</p></article>
          <article class="area-zone-item"><h3><a href="/loft-conversion-cambridge/">Cambridge</a></h3><p>Full Cambridge and surrounding village coverage as part of our Cambridgeshire service.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="area-section">
      <div class="area-wrap">
        <div class="area-head">
          <h2>Why March Homeowners Choose Truleum</h2>
          <p>Homeowners in March and across the Fenland district choose us for reliable results, clear pricing and quality workmanship on every project.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="area-proof-grid">
          <article class="area-proof"><i class="fas fa-map-marked-alt"></i><h3>Local Team</h3><p>Strong understanding of Fenland housing, planning context and site requirements in March.</p></article>
          <article class="area-proof"><i class="fas fa-file-signature"></i><h3>Transparent Quotes</h3><p>Written quotes with clear inclusions and no surprise costs at any stage of the project.</p></article>
          <article class="area-proof"><i class="fas fa-shield-alt"></i><h3>Fully Insured</h3><p>Complete professional insurance coverage throughout every stage of your loft conversion.</p></article>
          <article class="area-proof"><i class="fas fa-award"></i><h3>Quality Finish</h3><p>Careful attention to detail creates a finished space that is practical, well built and lasting.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="area-section area-faq">
      <div class="area-wrap">
        <div class="area-head">
          <h2>March Cambridgeshire Loft Conversion FAQs</h2>
          <p>Common questions from March homeowners. Our <a href="/loft-conversion-cost-cambridge/" style="color: var(--area-blue); font-weight:600;">cost guide</a> has full pricing detail for Cambridgeshire projects.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="area-faq-grid">
          <article class="area-faq-item">
            <h3>How much does a loft conversion in March cost?</h3>
            <p>Most projects in March range from £26,000 to £58,000 depending on conversion type, structural requirements and finishing specification. We provide a written quote after a free site survey with no obligation to proceed.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="area-faq-item">
            <h3>Are Fenland terraces in March suitable for loft conversions?</h3>
            <p>Yes. Most traditional terraces and semis in March have roof spaces that convert well. Dormer and Velux conversions are both common in this type of housing. We assess each property individually during the free survey.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="area-faq-item">
            <h3>Do I need planning permission for a loft conversion in March?</h3>
            <p>Many loft conversions in March are covered by permitted development rights and do not require a planning application. Properties in conservation areas or with major roof changes may need permission. We advise clearly on this from the outset.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="area-faq-item">
            <h3>How long does a loft conversion in March take?</h3>
            <p>A typical build runs from 6 to 10 weeks from the start date, depending on the conversion type chosen and any structural work required.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="area-cta">
      <div class="area-wrap">
        <p style="margin:0 0 12px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.82);">Useful links: <a href="/loft-conversion-glossary/" style="color:#ffe89f; font-weight:600;">Loft Conversion Glossary</a> | <a href="/loft-conversion-cost-cambridge/" style="color:#ffe89f; font-weight:600;">Cost Guide</a> | <a href="/loft-conversion-cambridge-guide-for-homeowners/" style="color:#ffe89f; font-weight:600;">Homeowner Guide</a> | <a href="/loft-conversion-cambridge/" style="color:#ffe89f; font-weight:600;">Cambridge Area Page</a></p>
        <h2>Plan Your March Loft Conversion Today</h2>
        <p>Book a free site survey to discuss your project, explore layout options and understand the costs. We will help you create extra space that works for your home.</p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="area-btn area-btn-primary">Book Free Consultation <i class="fas fa-calendar-check"></i></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much does a loft conversion in March cost?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Most projects in March, Cambridgeshire range from £26,000 to £58,000 depending on conversion type, structural requirements and finishing level."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Are Fenland terraces in March suitable for loft conversions?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Most traditional terraces and semis in March convert well. Dormer and Velux options are both common for this type of Fenland housing."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do I need planning permission for a loft conversion in March?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Many conversions in March are covered by permitted development. Conservation areas or major roof changes may require a planning application."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does a loft conversion in March take?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A typical build in March takes 6 to 10 weeks from start, depending on conversion type and structural requirements."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
    </script>

  </main>
</BaseLayout>
